third_party/fairplay-sap is the FairPlay SAP sender from
https://github.com/objevovat/fairplay-sap-core-airplay2-sender-authentication-handshake,
reduced to its C port and a C++ port of its Go packages, and is licensed under
LGPL-3.0-or-later. Its LGPL parts derive from Omar Roth's doubletake,
https://github.com/omarroth/doubletake (commit 8ccea5f), which is also
LGPL-3.0. The C++ port was made for this project on 2026-11-15. See LICENSE,
COPYING.GPL-3.0, and NOTICE.md in that directory. tests/fairplay_vectors.inc
holds output of that module and carries
the same license. The OBS plugin compiles that code in. The combined work is
distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later.

Pairing uses the public SRP-6a and HomeKit TLV descriptions. That code is part
of this project and is not taken from the LGPL module.

third_party/tweetnacl is TweetNaCl 20140427, which is in the public domain, by
Daniel J. Bernstein, Bernard van Gastel, Wesley Janssen, Tanja Lange, Peter
Schwabe, and Sjaak Smetsers. It supplies Ed25519 and X25519 for one-time
pairing. This project provides randombytes and builds that file with a 32-bit
u32 so the hash stays correct on 64-bit macOS.
